※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4415 LANG_MATCH_BOTTOM_NEEDS_A_RESULT

※ A sum names its alternatives by their types, so every arm of one is written
※ with a type.  `⊥` exists because a result's two alternatives may name one
※ type and so cannot both be said by naming one.

type Number = whole : i64 | fraction : f64

fn which(n: Number) → u8:
    match n:
        i64(w):
            return 1u8
        ⊥:
            return 2u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
